"DAL-006 Confidential Cover Sheet and Declaration re Documents for Stay and Early Evaluation Conference (Disability Access Litigation) (https://courts.ca.gov/sites/default/files/courts/default/2024-11/dal006.pdf)\nciteturn1655search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.4 years ago; Crawled: last year; CONFIDENTIAL  DAL-006 ... SUPERIOR COURT OF CALIFORNIA, COUNTY OF\nCONFIDENTIAL  DAL-006\n\nATTORNEY OR PARTY WITHOUT ATTORNEY (Name, State Bar number of attorney, and address):\nTELEPHONE NO.:  FAX NO.:\nE-MAIL ADDRESS (Optional):\nATTORNEY FOR (Name):\n\nSUPERIOR COURT OF CALIFORNIA, COUNTY OF\nSTREET ADDRESS:\nMAILING ADDRESS:\nCITY AND ZIP CODE:\nBRANCH NAME:\n\nPLAINTIFF:\nDEFENDANT:\n\nFOR COURT USE ONLY\n\nCASE NUMBER:\n\nCONFIDENTIAL COVER SHEET AND DECLARATION RE DOCUMENTS  \nFOR STAY AND EARLY EVALUATION CONFERENCE\n\nThis Confidential Cover Sheet and Declaration should be affixed to the first page of any of the documents listed below. It may not be used with other documents.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS TO CLERK: Certain supporting documents to be filed along with or following an Application for Stay of Proceedings and Early Evaluation Conference are to be kept confidential, as provided by Civil Code sections 55.54(c)(6) and (d)(4)(A) and (5). Such document are not to be made part of the public record except to the extent provided in Civil Code section 55.54(e)(4).\n\nAttached hereto is a true and correct copy of one or more of the following documents (check all that apply):\n\n1. ☐ Report issued by a Certified Access Specialist on a site that is the subject of this litigation. (This document may become publicly accessible at some point, under Civil Code section 55.54(e)(4).)\n2. ☐ Wage report forms filed by defendant with the Employment Development Department.\n3. ☐ State or federal income tax returns filed by defendant.\n\nI declare under penalty of perjury under the laws of the State of California that the foregoing is true and correct.\n\nDate:\n\n______________________________      ______________________________\n(TYPE OR PRINT NAME OF DECLARANT)      (SIGNATURE OF DECLARANT)\n\nPage 1 of 1\n\nForm Adopted for Mandatory Use  \nJudicial Council of California  \nDAL-006 [Rev. July 1, 2013]\n\nCONFIDENTIAL COVER SHEET AND DECLARATION RE DOCUMENTS  \nFOR STAY AND EARLY EVALUATION CONFERENCE  \n(Disability Access Litigation)\n\nCivil Code, § 55.54\n\nFor your protection and privacy, please press the Clear This Form button after you have printed the form.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJudicial Council of California . Administrative Office of the Courts (https://courts.ca.gov/sites/default/files/courts/default/2024-12/jc-20121214-itema2.pdf)\nciteturn1655search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; CONFIDENTIAL ATTORNEY OR PARTY WITHOUT ATTORNEY (Name, State Bar number of attorney, and address): TELEPHONE NO.: FAX NO.: E-MAIL ADDRESS: ATTORNEY FOR (Name): | DAL-006 FOR COURT USE ONLY DRAFT 11/29/12 Not approved by Judicial Council ... www.courts.ca.gov\nCONFIDENTIAL\nDAL-006\nCONFIDENTIAL ATTORNEY OR PARTY WITHOUT ATTORNEY (Name, State Bar number of attorney, and address): TELEPHONE NO.: FAX NO.: E-MAIL ADDRESS: ATTORNEY FOR (Name): | DAL-006 FOR COURT USE ONLY DRAFT 11/29/12 Not approved by Judicial Council\n--- | ---\nCONFIDENTIAL SUPERIOR COURT OF CALIFORNIA, COUNTY OF STREET ADDRESS: MAILING ADDRESS: CITY AND ZIP CODE: BRANCH NAME: | DAL-006 None\nCONFIDENTIAL CONFIDENTIAL COVER SHEET AND DECLARATION RE DOCUMENTS FOR STAY AND EARLY EVALUATION CONFERENCE | DAL-006 CASE NUMBER:\nThis Confidential Cover Sheet and Declaration should be affixed to the first page of any of the documents listed \nbelow.  It may not be used with other documents.\nINSTRUCTIONS TO CLERK: Certain supporting documents to be filed along with or following an Application for Stay of \nProceedings and Early Evaluation Conference are to be kept confidential, as provided by Civil Code sections \n55.54(b)(2)(C)(6) and 55.54(d)(4)–(5).  Such document are not  to be made part of the public record except to the extent \nprovided in Civil Code section 55.54(e)(4). \n Attached hereto is a true and correct copy of one or more of the following documents (check all that apply): \n1.\nReport issued by a Certified Access Specialist on a site that is the subject of this litigation.  (This document may \nbecome publicly accessible at some point, under Civil Code section 55.54(e)(4).)\n2.\nWage report forms filed by defendant with the Employment  Development Department.\nState or federal income tax returns filed by defendant.\n3.\nI declare under penalty of perjury under the laws of the State of California that the foregoing is true and correct. \nDate:\n(SIGNATURE OF DECLARANT)\n(TYPE OR PRINT NAME OF DECLARANT)\nPage 1 of 1\nCivil Code, § 55.54\nwww.courts.ca.gov\nForm Approved  for Mandatory Use \nJudicial Council of California \nDAL-006 [New January 1, 2013]\nCONFIDENTIAL COVER SHEET AND DECLARATION RE DOCUMENTS \nFOR STAY AND EARLY EVALUATION CONFERENCE \n(Disability Access Litigation)\n \n12--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nConfidential Cover Sheet and Declaration re Documents for Stay and Early Evaluation Conference | California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/jcc-form/DAL-006)\nciteturn1655search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; # Confidential Cover Sheet and Declaration re Documents for Stay and Early Evaluation Conference (DAL-006)Tell the court clerk that documents you are filing with your Application for Stay of Proceedings and Early Evaluation Conference, Joint Inspection (DAL-005) are confidential.\n\n# Confidential Cover Sheet and Declaration re Documents for Stay and Early Evaluation Conference (DAL-006)\n\nTell the court clerk that documents you are filing with your Application for Stay of Proceedings and Early Evaluation Conference, Joint Inspection (DAL-005) are confidential.\n\nGet form D